#### rejects embedded values that cross declared document boundaries

- Verify: rejects embedded values that cross declared document boundaries


<details>
<summary>Executable SSpec</summary>

Runnable source: 13 lines folded for reproduction.
Reproduction: this block contains the complete executable scenario source.

```simple
# @req: REQ-SSPEC-LOCAL-001
step("Verify: rejects embedded values that cross declared document boundaries")
val r = bson_decode(_bad_embedded_int32_crosses_boundary())
assert_equal(r.is_ok(), false)
match r:
    case Err(e):
        match e:
            case BsonError.UnexpectedEnd:
                assert_equal(true, true)
            case _:
                assert_equal(false, true)
    case _:
        assert_equal(false, true)
```

</details>

#### keeps valid empty strings

- Verify: keeps valid empty strings


<details>
<summary>Executable SSpec</summary>

Runnable source: 13 lines folded for reproduction.
Reproduction: this block contains the complete executable scenario source.

```simple
step("Verify: keeps valid empty strings")
# @req: REQ-SSPEC-LOCAL-001
val r = bson_decode(_valid_empty_string())
assert_equal(r.is_ok(), true)
match r.unwrap():
    case BsonValue.Doc(ps):
        match ps[0].1:
            case BsonValue.Str(s):
                assert_equal(s, "")
            case _:
                assert_equal(false, true)
    case _:
        assert_equal(false, true)
```

</details>

